title: 5. The readers the tier names read once each, Tay before Libby; each writes only what would change what gets built, or whether it can be followed.
pid: e2eeb71a-52ba-4cf0-a683-a0d523c6da2f
body: |2-
  Tay: is it worth doing, how far should it go, and which questions
  for Jeff does his taste answer. Libby: could a mind holding only the
  graph build each part from it, and could a later reader tell why each
  decision was made. There is no second round: the author's specialist folds the
  readings into the plan at the start of its first building mission,
  and a builder before it reads them with the plan.
  Why, and its sources: [[id:4b79a948-199d-430a-8047-e2ce67e67551][step 5, its reasons]].
